            "text": "Exactly right. Three of the four tiles are round, so P(round) = 3/4 = 75%. Each tile is equally likely to be drawn, so the most common shape wins — the order you dropped them in is irrelevant.\n\nA useful next check: what if you added one more square tile?\n\n```openui lifecycle=ephemeral id=tile-draw-new-square\n\nroot = LearningSurface([q], \"Add a square\", \"Predict the new odds before you look.\", \"ephemeral\")\nq = Question([{ header: \"New bag\", question: \"The bag now holds 5 tiles: 2 square and 3 round. Which shape is more likely to be drawn?\", type: \"choice\", choices: [\"Square\", \"Round\", \"Both are equally likely\"], allowText: true, hint: \"Compare the counts, then convert each to a fraction of 5.\" }], \"ephemeral\", \"Probability of a random draw\", \"Weigh the two counts against each other.\")\n\n```"
